{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 36, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262337.6934, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_c5d84a0f", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §1"], "detail": {"text": "Intermittent horizontal flicker or brightness pulsing on the Galaxy S24 main display typically occurs within seven days of a firmware update."}}
{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 37, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262337.8262, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_e272b8ae", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §1"], "detail": {"text": "The display flicker is usually visible at low brightness and on dark user interface themes."}}
{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 38, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262337.8945, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_58204bec", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §2"], "detail": {"text": "Ask the customer to disable Adaptive Brightness and Extra Dim, then observe for two minutes at 20 percent brightness."}}
{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 39, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262337.9998, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_ea109918", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §2"], "detail": {"text": "If the flicker stops, the cause is the adaptive brightness curve and a settings reset resolves it."}}
{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 40, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262338.078, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_a2b480a0", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §2"], "detail": {"text": "If the flicker persists, boot the device into Safe Mode."}}
{"session_id": "b3_dev_distract_01", "seq": 41, "t_rel_s": 4.139, "type": "claim_emitted", "wall_clock_ms": 1790441262338.135, "intent_id": "int_33b3c67e", "claim_id": "clm_1cda0155", "citations": ["DOC_KB_01 §2"], "detail": {"text": "Flicker that disappears in Safe Mode indicates a third-party application overlay rather than a panel fault."}}
